// @run
// @log 3
// @log 1
// GRADUATED (silent-class-inventory D47). This file pinned the `-3` map-value floor for
// three merges; it now pins the LIFT, and the condition table below is what it measured
// while it was a floor. Renamed from `error-map-value-struct-in-union.vl` — the reject it
// was named for is gone.
//
// A STRUCT that is a MEMBER of a declared union, as a map VALUE, spelled INLINE at the
// binding. What used to reject here — under both key reps — is exactly what the ALIAS
// spelling has run since D34, and D-ALIASMAP says the two must not differ.
//
// THE CONDITION IT PINNED, six cells per key rep, measured when this was a floor:
//
//     struct-valued map ALONE                                        runs
//     union-valued map ALONE                                         runs
//     struct-valued map + a DISJOINT union-valued map (`{[K]: T|U}`)  RUNS
//     struct-valued map + an OVERLAPPING union-valued map (`S|T`)    rejected
//     struct-valued map + a union ALIAS `S | T`, NO union-valued map rejected
//     the same overlap through a LIST of maps                        rejected
//
// The two that rejected are the two where `S` is a MEMBER of a declared union, and the
// fifth line is the one that killed the ORIGINAL (#1286) framing: there is no union-valued
// map in this file at all. The pair was never the condition.
//
// THE MECHANISM, AND THE CORRECTION D47 MADE TO IT. `mvValKindOfName`'s last arm is
// `structIndexByValName(valName) >= 0`, a `sNames` lookup — and `collectS` SKIPS a
// `type X = {…}` that is a union member, so declaring `S | T` DELETES `S`'s struct row and
// the arm missed. The row's filed note said the ALIAS spelling escaped because the alias
// declaration interned the render `{x:i32}` as an inline-shape row first; MEASURED, that is
// wrong — declaring `type M = {[string]: S}` without USING it leaves this program rejecting.
// What the alias actually changes is the SPELLING that reaches the mv layer: a TypeRef's
// emit name for an alias is `tyToEmitName` of the resolved type, which renders the arm
// structurally, while the inline annotation hands over the source text `S`.
//
// THE FIX KEYS BOTH SPELLINGS ON THE ARM'S OWN NAME (`mvArmKeyName`), read off the caller's
// recorded type by DECLARATION identity — the one channel both spellings have. Nominal, so
// a genuinely anonymous `{[string]: {x:i32}}` is untouched.
type S = { x: i32 }
type T = { y: i32 }
type Q = S | T
function go() {
  const a: {[string]: S} = Map()
  a["k"] = { x: 1 }
  const q: Q = { y: 3 }
  if q is T { print(q.y) }
  print(a.length)
}
go()
